  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "jungle: the Amen's first bar answered by a chopped second bar, the snare stuttering into a roll at its end, over a long booming sub that walks root, fifth, fourth, root",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: the first is the break as written, the second is a re-edit (kick one, one-and, three-and, snares on two, two-a, three-e and then a sixteenth roll from four) — the chopping jungle producers did on a sampler, here as steps. The sub notes are long and far apart, which is where jungle leaves the space the break fills."
  }
